Alembic migrations for the EarnIt backend
=========================================

Single-database, async configuration. How this setup differs from the stock
Alembic template (all wiring lives in `env.py`):

- Database URL: taken from `src.core.config.settings.database_url` (built from
  the POSTGRES_* env vars / `.env`), NOT from the `sqlalchemy.url` placeholder
  in `alembic.ini`. That placeholder is ignored.
- Target metadata: `SQLModel.metadata`. `env.py` imports `src.models` so every
  table is registered before autogenerate runs — a new model must be reachable
  from that package or autogenerate won't see it.
- Migrations run against an async engine (asyncpg); both online and offline
  modes are supported.
- `render_item` renders SQLModel's `AutoString` as plain `sa.String`, so the
  generated migration files don't import `sqlmodel`.

Common commands
---------------

Inside the running stack (the `api` container reaches Postgres over the compose
network, so this is the usual path):

    docker compose exec api uv run alembic upgrade head        # apply latest
    docker compose exec api uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "msg"
    docker compose exec api uv run alembic downgrade -1        # roll back one
    docker compose exec api uv run alembic current             # show revision

Locally (without Docker), with `.env` pointing at a reachable Postgres
(`POSTGRES_HOST=localhost`):

    uv run alembic upgrade head

Always review an autogenerated revision before committing it — autogenerate
does not detect every change (e.g. some constraint/type edits) and may need
hand-editing.
